==============================================================================
M-004  neckline = sum(troughs)/2.0  --  it scales with the COUNT, not
       the location, of the troughs between the shoulders
==============================================================================
  2 troughs  85 / 86               -> hit index=10 neckline=85.5000 strength=1.0000
  3 troughs  85 / 86 / 86.5        -> hit index=10 neckline=128.7500 strength=1.0000
  4 troughs  85 / 86 / 86.5 / 87   -> hit index=10 neckline=172.2500 strength=1.0000

  the same three troughs re-scored by the formula the code uses:
    2 troughs: sum/2.0 =  85.5000   true mean =  85.5000   head 100 minus it =  14.5000
    3 troughs: sum/2.0 = 128.7500   true mean =  85.8333   head 100 minus it = -28.7500
    4 troughs: sum/2.0 = 172.2500   true mean =  86.1250   head 100 minus it = -72.2500
  -> with 3 or more inter-shoulder troughs the neckline is ABOVE the
     head, so `closes[j] < neckline` can never be satisfied and the
     detector silently returns None for the rest of the run.  The
     auditor's phrasing ('mean of all troughs') understates it: the
     divisor is a hard-coded 2.0, not len(between).

